# Netlify response headers (2026-11-03, his go on the blog speed fix).
# Photos had "max-age=0, must-revalidate", so every visit re-checked every image with the server.
# Browsers may now keep them for a day (fresh), and for up to a week after that may show the
# copy they have once while they fetch the new one in the background (stale-while-revalidate).
# So a photo replaced under the SAME filename can show its old version to a returning visitor:
# for up to a day, then for one more view any time within the following week. Replacement
# photos should get new filenames (the pipeline names new photos fresh). A deploy refreshes
# Netlify's own servers, not visitors' browsers.
/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/blog/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800
